.TH ag-remote-import-issues 1  "import-issues 0.3.0-beta.7"
.SH NAME
ag\-remote\-import\-issues \- Preview or explicitly apply a normalized GitHub/GitLab issue manifest
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBag remote import\-issues\fR [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-remote\fR] [\fB\-\-apply\fR] [\fB\-\-as\fR] [\fB\-\-expected\-digest\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-unsupported\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fB\-\-file\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Preview or explicitly apply a normalized GitHub/GitLab issue manifest
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Operate on the repository at this path (default: discovered from the current directory)
.TP
\fB\-\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Normalized GitHub/GitLab issue manifest (UTF\-8 JSON, at most 4 MiB)
.TP
\fB\-\-remote\fR \fI<REMOTE>\fR
Remote to use (default: origin)
.TP
\fB\-\-apply\fR
Apply the manifest instead of only previewing it
.TP
\fB\-\-as\fR \fI<IDENTITY>\fR
Act as this identity (`user:alice`, `agent:bot#run_…`, `service:ci`). Also: AG_IDENTITY
.TP
\fB\-\-expected\-digest\fR \fI<DIGEST>\fR
Exact digest returned by the preview of this manifest
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Machine\-readable JSON output
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-unsupported\fR
Acknowledge unsupported source features listed in the preview
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR
Colour the output: auto (a terminal, unless NO_COLOR is set), always or never
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print only what was asked for: no confirmations or hints. Errors and refusals are still shown
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Explain what is happening on standard error: repository, identity, remote, timing
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH VERSION
v0.3.0\-beta.7
